Today is Saturday morning.
I am volunteering at the café.
Many people come into the café to avoid getting wet in the rain.
Because of that, there is a huge rush in the café today.
Jessy and I are working fast.
We do not need to talk much.
We know very well what to do now.
"Two coffees to the fourth table," Jessy calls out.
"I will take it," I reply.
I place the coffee on their table.
After that, I wipe the next table quickly.
People are drinking hot tea and watching the rain.
It is warm and busy inside the café.
Jessy prepares the orders, and I serve them.
We are working as a good team.
Compared to the first days, this work is very easy for me now.
